<title>MALAYSIA: SQUASH-WOMEN'S WORLD TEAM CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SQUASH-WOMEN'S WORLD TEAM CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PETALING JAYA, Malaysia 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the</p>
<p>women's world team squash championships on Wednesday:</p>
<p>Pool A</p>
<p>Australia beat United States 3-0</p>
<p>Sarah Fitz-Gerald beat Demer Holleran 9-1 9-6 9-2</p>
<p>Liz Irving beat Alicia McConnell 9-2 2-2, McConnell retired</p>
<p>injured</p>
<p>Carol Owens beat Berkeley Belknap 9-2 9-1 9-1</p>
<p>South Africa beat Germany 2-1 (South African names first)</p>
<p>Claire Nitch lost to Sabine Schone 7-9 9-4 6-9 6-9</p>
<p>Carla Venter beat Sabine Baum 9-7 6-9 9-5 2-9 9-3</p>
<p>Chantal Clifton-Parks beat Karin Beriere 9-4 10-8 9-1</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>England beat New Zealand 2-1 (English names first)</p>
<p>Cassie Jackman beat Philippa Beams 7-9 9-7 9-1 8-10 9-2</p>
<p>Suzanne Horner lost to Leilani Marsh 2-9 2-9 2-9</p>
<p>Linda Charman beat Sarah Cook 10-8 9-1 2-9 6-9 9-4</p>
<p>Netherlands beat Egypt 3-0</p>
<p>Vanessa Atkinson beat Salma Shabana 9-3 9-5 9-3</p>
<p>Nicole Beumer beat Maha Zein 9-1 9-4 9-1</p>
<p>Denise Sommers beat Heba Abu Ouf 9-3 5-9 9-5 9-2</p>
<p>Pool C</p>
<p>Canada beat Ireland 3-0</p>
<p>Hether Wallace beat Ailing McArdle 9-0 9-2 9-3</p>
<p>Melanie Jans beat Louise Finnegand 9-4 5-9 9-0 6-9 10-8</p>
<p>Kelsey Souchereau beat Olivia French 9-5 9-5 9-5</p>
<p>Finland beat Malaysia 3-0</p>
<p>Tuula Myllyniemi beat Leong Siu Lynn 9-7 9-6 9-1</p>
<p>Nina Taimiaho beat Kuan Choy Lin 9-0 1-9 9-4 5-9 9-5</p>
<p>Kia Passivirta beat Carrie Yeo 9-3 9-3 9-1</p>
<p>Pool D</p>
<p>Scotland beat France 3-0</p>
<p>Senga Macfie beat Corinne Castets 4-9 9-4 9-5 9-2</p>
<p>Claire Waddell beat Isabelle Stoehr 8-10 9-4 9-0 10-8</p>
<p>Wendy Maitland beat Corinne Vezin 9-4 9-0 9-5</p>
<p>Hong Kong beat Japan 2-1 (Hong Kong names first)</p>
<p>Dawn Olsen beat Yoko Kimura 9-0 7-9 9-4 9-5</p>
<p>Rebecca Chiu beat Misako Sugo 9-5 9-3 9-0</p>
<p>Iris Chung lost to Yuriko Sakai 3-9 0-9 6-9</p>
<p>Pool E</p>
<p>Brazil beat Italy 3-0</p>
<p>Flavia Roberts beat Sonia Pasteris 0-9 9-3 3-9 9-3 9-0</p>
<p>Adriana Moura beat Elena Cambi 9-0 9-2 4-9 9-1</p>
<p>Mariana Pontalti beat Anna Sterchele 9-5 9-3 9-0</p>
<p>Denmark beat Spain 2-1 (Danish names first)</p>
<p>Ellen Hamborg-Peterson lost to Natalie Meneu 7-9 9-6 2-9 0-9</p>
<p>Julie Dorn-Jensen beat Elisabet Sado 9-4 3-9 5-9 9-2 9-6</p>
<p>Elsbeth Jensen beat Nuria Salvia 8-10 9-5 9-3 10-8</p>
</text>
